<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chartres</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Autricum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chartres is a city on the River <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eure">Eure</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the Gallo-Roman Autricum, chief town of the Carnutes. It later became a seat of the counts of Blois and a centre of learning in the 11th and 12th centuries. Its cathedral, rebuilt after a fire of 1194 with outstanding stained glass, is one of the finest Gothic churches and a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chartres.jpg" alt="Chartres" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ludvig14 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chartres_DJI_0352a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
